= Mentor Path
Apache Incubator PMC
2025-09-29
:jbake-type: guide
:jbake-status: published
:idprefix:
:toc:
:imagesdir: ../../images/

== Mentor Learning Path

Mentors play a critical role in helping podlings learn the Apache Way.  
This path introduces the core responsibilities and provides exercises to practice.

**New to mentoring?** You’re not expected to read everything at once. Start with the link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Incubator+Mentor+Quick+Start+Guide[Mentor Quick Start Guide] and use the rest as reference when you need it.

This link:https://youtu.be/2LV6Uk4K-wA[short video] welcomes new mentors to the Apache Incubator and provides an overview of the process for getting started.

See also: link:../index.html[Training Home] | link:../resources.html[All Resources]

[.small]
*Key:* 📘 Guide 🖥️ Slide Deck 🎞️ Video 🧩 Quiz 🧠 Practice / Scenario 🎮 Interactive

== Steps

1. 📘 **Read:** link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Incubator+Mentor+Quick+Start+Guide[Mentor Quick Start Guide] - fast orientation for new mentors  
2. 📘 **Read:** link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Mentor+Onboarding[Mentor Onboarding] - detailed overview of mentor responsibilities and expectations  
3. 🎞️ **Watch:** link:https://youtu.be/kdxCJY97vZA[Mentor Onboarding] - video of Mentor Onboarding presentation  
4. 🧩 **Quiz:** link:https://canvas.instructure.com/enroll/JHL8BM[ASF Mentor Onboarding Quiz]  
5. 🧠 **Practice:** link:https://canvas.instructure.com/enroll/GXPFY3[Mentor Scenarios Training]  
6. 📘 **Read:** link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Best+Practices+for+Mentors[Best Practices for Mentors] - real-world mentoring examples and scenarios  
7. 📘 **Read:** link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Incubator+Case+Studies[Incubator Case Studies] - lessons learned from past podlings  
8. 📘 **Read:** link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Mentors+Tough+Conversation+Guide[Mentors’ Tough Conversation Guide] - approaches for handling challenging situations  

---
== Also see

📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Mentor+Handbook[Mentor Handbook] - the central reference tying together all mentor responsibilities, guidance, and training materials. Start here before exploring individual topics below.

=== Orientation & Fundamentals
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/IPMC+Oversight[IPMC Oversight] - how the IPMC provides high-level oversight, guidance, and course correction across podlings  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Incubation+Explained[Incubation Explained] - overview of the Incubator’s purpose, practices, and lessons learned  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Podling+Orientation+Guide[Podling Orientation Guide] - introduction to the incubation process and expectations for new podlings  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Who+Does+What[Who Does What] - clarifies roles and responsibilities across the ASF, IPMC, mentors, and podling PMCs  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Why+Governance+Matters[Why Governance Matters] - explains why governance is central to ASF culture and how mentors help podlings apply it  
- 🖥️ link:https://training.apache.org/presentations/apache/incubator/ASFvalues/index.html[ASF Values] - introduction to the core cultural values of the ASF  
- 🎞️ link:https://youtu.be/d9XFK3ZLr8I[ASF Values] - video overview of ASF Values  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Incubation+Readiness[Incubation Readiness] - patterns seen when projects are (and are not) ready to enter incubation  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Proposal+Discussions[Proposal Discussions] - what typically comes up during proposal threads and reviews  

=== Mentoring, Stewardship & Community Building
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Joining+the+Incubator[Joining the Incubator] - what prospective podlings should know before applying and how mentors can guide them through the proposal process  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Mentor+Onboarding[Mentor Onboarding] - guidance on the responsibilities and expectations of new mentors  
- 🎞️ link:https://youtu.be/kdxCJY97vZA[Mentor Onboarding] - video of Mentor Onboarding presentation  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Mentor+Offboarding[Mentor Offboarding] - guidance on stepping back and handing off mentoring responsibilities  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Selecting+a+PMC+Chair[Selecting a PMC Chair] - guidance on choosing a balanced and effective PMC Chair  
- 🖥️ link:https://training.apache.org/presentations/apache/incubator/CommunityBuilding/index.html[Community Building in Practice (Slide Deck)] - building and sustaining healthy, diverse communities  
- 🎞️ link:https://youtu.be/rCkqAn6f19Y[Community Building in Practice] - how mentors can help podlings turn contributors into a sustainable Apache community  
- 🎮 link:https://incubator.apache.org/training/scenarios/[Mentoring in Practice] - interactive, story-based exercises that help mentors explore real-world incubation challenges  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Community+Governance[Community Governance] - recurring governance issues mentors commonly help resolve  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Initial+Committer+Selection[Initial Committer Selection] - early committer decisions and their long-term impact on governance  

=== Governance, Consensus & Neutrality
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Governance+in+Practice[Governance in Practice] - guidance on applying ASF governance principles in podling communities  
- 🖥️ link:https://training.apache.org/presentations/apache/incubator/Governance/index.html[Governance in Practice (Slide Deck)] - how ASF governance works day to day  
- 🎞️ link:https://youtu.be/fMcasCOImyQ[Governance in Practice] - turning ASF principles into everyday project practice  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Common+Myths[Common Myths About the Incubator] - corrects frequent misunderstandings about incubation, reporting, and decision-making  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Voting+and+Consensus+in+Practice[Voting and Consensus in Practice] - how consensus and voting shape decision-making in ASF projects  
- 🖥️ link:https://training.apache.org/presentations/apache/incubator/VotingAndConsensus/index.html[Voting and Consensus in Practice (Slide Deck)] - understanding how Apache communities make decisions  
- 🎞️ link:https://youtu.be/hdBaPzeCyk0[Voting and Consensus in Practice] - how ASF projects make transparent, inclusive, and consensus-driven decisions  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Communication+in+Apache+Projects[Communication in Apache Projects] - helping podlings use mailing lists and chats transparently and effectively  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Vendor+Neutrality[Vendor Neutrality] - ensuring projects remain independent of single-vendor control  
- 📘link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Neutrality+In+Practice[Neutrality In Practice] — practical guidance on how incubating projects maintain community-led, vendor-neutral governance
- 🖥️ link:https://training.apache.org/presentations/apache/incubator/VendorNeutrality/index.html[Vendor Neutrality (Slide Deck)] - why balanced governance keeps Apache projects healthy and independent  
- 🎞️ link:https://youtu.be/WmmZYl3ZNr0[Vendor Neutrality] - how mentors can help podlings maintain a balanced and independent community  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Edge+Cases[Edge Cases] - uncommon or ambiguous situations raised during incubation  

=== Branding, Legal & Infrastructure
- 🖥️ link:https://training.apache.org/presentations/apache/incubator/BrandingIdentity/index.html[Branding & Identity (Slide Deck)] - guidance on name use, logo policy, and protecting ASF trademarks  
- 🎞️ link:https://youtu.be/EsrPHkDhNTU[Branding & Identity] - how mentors can guide podlings to follow ASF branding and identity policies  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Third-Party+Branding+Incubating+Projects[Third-Party Branding and Incubating Projects] - using third-party brands while respecting ASF branding policies  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Legal+Basics[Legal Basics] - ensuring podling releases meet ASF legal and licensing requirements  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Interacting+with+ASF+Infra[Interacting with ASF Infrastructure] - when and how mentors can help podlings engage with ASF Infra  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Naming+and+Branding[Naming and Branding] - identity and presentation issues that arise during incubation  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Naming+and+Trademarks[Naming and Trademarks] - trademark-related questions raised in practice  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Licensing+and+Provenance[Licensing and Provenance] - recurring licensing and source-origin concerns  

=== Reporting, Graduation & Beyond
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/TRAINING/ASF+Project+Reporting+Guidance[Project Report Guide] - guidance on preparing and submitting ASF project reports to the Board  
- 🧠 link:https://canvas.instructure.com/enroll/EM7DCX[Incubator Reporting Scenarios] - interactive practice on writing and evaluating podling reports  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Measuring+Podling+Health[Measuring Podling Health] - how mentors evaluate community activity, diversity, and engagement  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Release+Vote+Insights[Release Vote Insights] - analysis of vote patterns and lessons from past release reviews to improve mentoring and podling readiness  

==== Releases
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Releases[Releases] - practical release issues that come up during incubation  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Release+Review+Issues[Release Review Issues] - recurring problems found during podling release reviews  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Release+Announcements[Release Announcements] - practical guidance on announcing podling releases  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Release+Votes[Release Votes] - patterns and lessons from release vote discussions  

==== Graduation
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Graduation+Criteria[Graduation Criteria] - requirements and checks for graduation readiness  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Graduation+Readiness[Graduation Readiness] - issues that commonly surface late in incubation  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Graduation+Identity[Graduation Identity] - branding and public-identity concerns at graduation  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Graduation+Votes[Graduation Votes] - how graduation discussions typically unfold  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Graduation+and+Beyond[Graduation and Beyond] - guidance on the post-graduation transition and ongoing relationship with the ASF  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/How+To+Use+the+ASF+Maturity+Model[How To Use the ASF Maturity Model] - framework for assessing podling readiness and project health  

=== Lessons & Case Studies
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Incubator+Case+Studies[Incubator Case Studies] - examples of challenges and successes from past podlings  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Practicing+The+Apache+Way[Practicing The Apache Way] - scenario-based cases from real Incubator situations (anonymized)
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Incubator+Discussion+Trends[Incubator Discussion Trends] - long-term patterns in general@ list topics over ten years  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Mentor+Engagement+Patterns[Mentor Engagement Patterns] - data-driven analysis of mentor participation, sign-offs, and responsiveness  
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Mentor+Trends[Mentor Trends] - common podling issues and mentoring patterns from recent report analysis
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Incubator+Health[Incubator Health] - long-term system-wide health indicators across the Incubator
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/10+years+of+the+Incubator[10 Years of the Incubator] — a decade-long retrospective on Incubator growth, scale, challenges, and governance evolution
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/10+Years+Summary[10 Years Summary] - summary of ten years of Incubator trends, impacts, and governance evolution
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/IPMC+Governance[IPMC Governance] - long-term analysis of incubator-general governance activity, participation continuity, and how governance load scales with podling population
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Governance+Patterns[Governance Patterns] — cross-podling study of mailing-list activity revealing common governance-development trajectories and warning signals during incubation
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Podling+Governance+Patterns[Podling Governance Patterns] — observed patterns in how podlings develop governance during incubation, based on long-term analysis of public mailing-list activity and podling outcomes
- 📘 link:https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/INCUBATOR/Community+and+Governance+Growth[Community and Governance Growth] — ten-year empirical study of how podlings build sustainable community and governance over time: key healthy growth trajectories and common risk signals
